SSC CGL – Trigonometry (त्रिकोणमिति) Notes

-------------------------
🔹 Basic Trigonometric Ratios
-------------------------

1. sin θ = perpendicular / hypotenuse
2. cos θ = base / hypotenuse
3. tan θ = perpendicular / base = sin θ / cos θ
4. cot θ = 1 / tan θ = base / perpendicular
5. sec θ = 1 / cos θ = hypotenuse / base
6. cosec θ = 1 / sin θ = hypotenuse / perpendicular

-------------------------
🔹 Standard Angles Table (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°)
-------------------------

| θ    | sin θ | cos θ | tan θ | cot θ | sec θ | cosec θ |
|------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|-----------|
| 0°   | 0      | 1      | 0      | ∞      | 1      | ∞         |
| 30°  | 1/2    | √3/2   | 1/√3   | √3     | 2/√3   | 2         |
| 45°  | 1/√2   | 1/√2   | 1      | 1      | √2     | √2        |
| 60°  | √3/2   | 1/2    | √3     | 1/√3   | 2      | 2/√3      |
| 90°  | 1      | 0      | ∞      | 0      | ∞      | 1         |

-------------------------
🔹 Trigonometric Identities
-------------------------

1. sin²θ + cos²θ = 1
2. 1 + tan²θ = sec²θ
3. 1 + cot²θ = cosec²θ

-------------------------
🔹 Angle Relationships
-------------------------

1. sin (90° – θ) = cos θ  
2. cos (90° – θ) = sin θ  
3. tan (90° – θ) = cot θ  
4. cot (90° – θ) = tan θ  
5. sec (90° – θ) = cosec θ  
6. cosec (90° – θ) = sec θ  

-------------------------
🔹 Trigonometric Values in Quadrants
-------------------------

- I Quadrant: All positive  
- II Quadrant: sin, cosec positive  
- III Quadrant: tan, cot positive  
- IV Quadrant: cos, sec positive  

-------------------------
🔹 Heights and Distances
-------------------------

- Use triangle formulas with angle of elevation/depression.
- Common angles: 30°, 45°, 60°

Examples:
1. Height = Base × tan θ
2. Distance = Height / tan θ

-------------------------
🔹 Tips for SSC CGL
-------------------------

- Memorize trigonometric values of standard angles.
- Practice identities and their manipulation.
- Solve problems involving angle of elevation and depression.
- Focus on quadrant signs (+/-).
- Use rationalization to simplify expressions.

-------------------------
🔹 Unit Circle Trick (Optional)
-------------------------

sin(180° – θ) = sin θ  
cos(180° – θ) = –cos θ  
tan(180° – θ) = –tan θ  

sin(360° – θ) = –sin θ  
cos(360° – θ) = cos θ  
tan(360° – θ) = –tan θ  

 